        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Species: Parnassius nordmanni\n- Plants: C. alpestris, C. conorhiza, C. emanueli, Cedrus\n- Places: Caucasus\n- Concepts: genus, naming system\n\nFacts:\n- Parnassius nordmanni is a high-altitude butterfly found in the Caucasus.\n- The larva of Parnassius nordmanni feeds on C. alpestris, C. conorhiza, and C. emanueli.\n- Cedrus is classified as a genus in the naming system.\n- C. alpestris, C. conorhiza, and C. emanueli are described as species in the chunk, and the chunk states that those species are classified as genus in the naming system.",
