        "original_id": "3f09d3fd-fa02-5568-b696-f94f7f152b87",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Taxa: Corydalis, Cedrus, Parnassius nordmanni\n- Plant families: Papaveraceae, Pinaceae\n- Topics: species diet, plant distribution\n\nFacts:\n- Corydalis is a genus of about 470 species of annual and perennial herbaceous plants in the Papaveraceae family.\n- Corydalis is native to the temperate Northern Hemisphere and the high mountains of tropical eastern Africa.\n- Cedrus, commonly called cedar in English, is a genus of coniferous trees in the Pinaceae family.\n- The larva of Parnassius nordmanni feeds on Corydalis species including C. alpestris, C. conorhiza, and C. emanueli.",
